<p>Hi,</p>
<% case @variant %>
<% when :no_source %>
<p>You signed up for Sessy a couple of days ago, but “<%= @account.name %>” doesn't have a source yet. A source is one SES configuration set you want to watch, and it's the first step to seeing your deliveries, bounces, and complaints.</p>
<p><%= link_to "Create your first source", @next_step_url %> — its Setup page then connects SES for you with a one-click Launch Stack button, no AWS console tour needed.</p>
<% when :no_subscription %>
<p>Your source “<%= @source.name %>” is still waiting for AWS: Sessy hasn't heard from SNS yet.</p>
<p>Open its <%= link_to "Setup page", @next_step_url %> and click <strong>Launch Stack</strong>. CloudFormation creates the configuration set, the SNS topic, and the event destination in your AWS account; Sessy shows “SNS connected” as soon as the subscription is confirmed.</p>
<p>Already created the stack? Check its Events tab in the CloudFormation console for a rollback, then try again from the Setup page.</p>
<% when :no_event %>
<p>SNS is connected to “<%= @source.name %>”, but Sessy hasn't received an event yet. That usually means nothing has been sent through the configuration set so far.</p>
<p>Send an email through the <code><%= @source.config_set_name %></code> configuration set, or make it the default for your sending identity with the command on the <%= link_to "Setup page", @next_step_url %>. Deliveries, bounces, and complaints show up moments later.</p>
<p>If your SES account is still in the sandbox, you can only send to verified addresses — a test to one of those is enough.</p>
<% end %>
<p style="color: #71717a; font-size: 14px;">Stuck or have questions? Just reply to this email and I'll help you out. This is the only reminder you'll get from us.</p>
